cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite it using the
  metadata below.
title: >-
  Analysis code: Quantitative spindle and chromosome dynamics in
  meiosis I, meiosis II and mitosis of Pyrrhocoris apterus
authors:
  - family-names: Lindner
    given-names: Alexander
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9570-1621"
  - family-names: Fabig
    given-names: Gunar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3017-0978"
  - family-names: Okafornta
    given-names: Chukwuebuka William
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8094-1254"
  - family-names: Müller-Reichert
    given-names: Thomas
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0203-1436"
version: v1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-28"
license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23020391"
abstract: >-
  Python notebook implementing the uniform windowed-linear speed analysis
  (bounded-logistic window finder + linear regression) for pole-to-pole,
  chromosome-to-chromosome and pole-to-chromosome distances in meiosis I,
  meiosis II and mitosis of Pyrrhocoris apterus, including anaphase A/B
  decomposition and the cell-size scaling analysis. Reproduces all
  quantitative results, figures and tables of the associated manuscript.
keywords:
  - mitosis
  - meiosis
  - spindle scaling
  - anaphase A
  - anaphase B
  - Pyrrhocoris apterus
  - holocentric chromosomes
repository-code: "https://github.com/gunar-f/firebug_spindle_analysis"
